I've written a few drivers for TURBOchannel in the past, but never needed
to know the difference in bus clock speed. So why do you want to know?

There is no information in the system which tells "This is a 12.5 MHz
TURBOchannel". The only way you can do this, is by using the cpu type
and knowing in your driver that this cpu has a 12.5 Meg TURBOchannel.

On ULTRIX you could do a check in global variable "cpu".
See /sys/machine/common/cpuconf.h. VMS has macros to find the cpu type...

/Peter
