I have a problem with FORTRAN carriage control in DEC FORTRAN.  In DEC
FORTRAN (under Ultrix), to get VMS style FORTRAN carriage control on a
terminal, you have to open unit 6 like this:

       open(unit=6,carriagecontrol='fortran',status='old')

After doing this, DEC's run time library translates all of the
ASA carriage control information written to unit 6 into carriage
returns, line feeds, etc.

This code:

       write(6,10)
       write(6,10)
 10    format(1x,'hello world',)

will produce:

<LF>hello world<CR><LF>hello world<CR>

which when passed through the terminal driver results in:

<CR><LF>hello world<CR><CR><LF>hello world<CR>

<CR> = carriage return
<LF> = line feed

Which should be fine, since two carriage returns in a row should
