In article <1993Jun26.022643.26574@hp9000.csc.cuhk.hk>, a866700@hp9000.csc.cuhk.hk (Wong Siu To) writes:
> Hi there,
> 
> We're going to integrate an DEC Alpha 3000/400S into our cluster with a
> MicroVAX 3400 running VMS 5.5 as the boot server.  Would anyone pls
> advise if there's any known or potential problem of a 'mixed' cluster ?
> Besides, I wonder how many software running on VAX/VMS is port to
> AXP/VMS, say compilers, TCP/IP for VMS (UCX), etc.

	The AXP will require it's own system disk (local!  Booting an AXP
off a VAX system can be done, but is not supported and requires tweaking
of several things).  OpenVMS AXP V1.5 should have no problem clustering
with your existing VAX 3400 system.

	There is lots of software that has been ported to AXP.  In general,
porting of software is not difficult.

	The biggest problem is simply dealing with a "homogenous" cluster
that requires two different images (one VAX and one AXP).  I have lots 
of symbols defined in SYLOGIN and my LOGIN that use F$GETSYI("ARCH_TYPE")
to define the correct symbol for the architecture.

