To phrase this delicately "Huh???" The DEUNA is a DIX Ethernet V2 device and
should work just fine with 802.3 transceivers, thick, thin, or twisted pair.
There is no need to modify the power supply or anything else. The DEUNA does
not have all the added ground pins specified for 802.3, but this should not
really be significant. This question could be better directed to
comp.dcom.lan.ethernet.

