Hi,

I don't know exactly what you mean with "register", but probably put them
in the moira database.

It all depends how you have included X-terminals in your environment:

1. If they are booting from an Infoserver or other system then the athena 
system, it's just a matter of doing a connect to the athena system from the
X-terminal.

2. If you want the X-terminals to be booted from the athena system, there
has to be a /etc/bootptab entry. However bootptab can get overwritten by dcm.
We solved this by creating  /etc/bootptab.local which get appended to 
/etc/bootptab. 
You have to include the following in /usr/athena/etc/decmipsboot.sh on 
the server:

Look for "if (! -e /etc/bootptab) exit $MR_NOBOOTFILE"
and put this after it:

if (-e /etc/bootptab.local) then
   echo "Appending local customizations to bootptabfile."
   cat /etc/bootptab.local >> /etc/bootptab
endif

However, you need an authenticated xdm, otherwise the user should be logged
already on the server in other to get his passwd entry in /etc/passwd. I've
seen a test version of an authenticated xdm, so be patient...

So to answer you original question: Moira is not capable of registering 
X-terminals. The question is should it do so? As an X-terminal is not a real
DECathena client and the password gets sent across the ethernet, although be
it embedded in an X-packet.....


