Except you are forgetting something. The RD54 is as high as the ST506
standard goes. It is the same thing with, say, MS630 memory. If you base
the value of a piece of equipment on one particular metric, then you run
into this thing called 'market value'. The MS630-BB memory board goes for
between $40 and $50 for 4megs. Using this ratio, you could say that the
MS630-CA 8meg board should go for $80 or $100, but it goes for twice that.

Don't forget about the RC25, either. The piece of junk only has 52meg
(is it even that much?) of storage, but it is still worth $800-$900 on
the used market. But by your estimation, it should not be worth shipping
it.

Getting back to the point, the 'market value' of a true RD54 (not an
XT2190) is about $400-500, so the original poster's price is not off
the wall.

