the board is good, the problem lies in the DECpc.

The LED staying on means 1) termination problem (clearly NOT the
problem here) or 2) the card is not "enabled" by the system BIOS
sending it the EISA configuration data (apparently the problem here).

After several days of frustration with DEC 800 numbers for support,
they concluded that my BIOS was downlevel (1.00.04).  The best the
800 support number people could offer was "place a service call"
(at several hundred dollars to fix THEIR problem on my machine!).

I ran into a local service rep for DEC who has been cooperative 
and got me a copy of the 1.00.05 BIOS update disk (to update the 
flash PROM for the bios).  That update went just fine but...

Now the SCU (EISA configuration diskette) does not recognize the
"hardware ID" of the CPU board.  It claims there is no config
(*.CFG) file for the CPU board.  With the old BIOS (1.00.04) the
CFG file was called !DEC1101.CFG.  That file apparently is now
invalid because the board now has the 1.00.05 bios code (?).

It would appear that I need the "current" SCU config program 
and/or *.CFG files for the 433ST with a 1.00.05 bios upgrade.

Remember, this is all to get the AHA1742 adapter installed and
configured.  DEC now sells this same card as an option in the 
4xxST family of PC's (still an active product.

