We had the opportunity to evaluate a 180 Mhz Alpha 3000 pre-launch box (as
the DEC sales people tell me).  They say the pre-launch box is 
pre-production so they might have performed some fine tuning on this box
to get some more speed out of it for the production boxes.  Anyway, we
benchmarked some of our in-house developed volume rendering software and
compared it against our 690MP with model 41 cpus.  The DEC rendered the
3D images right at twice as fast as our 690.  We are running SunOS 4.1.3 so
our software was running only on 1 cpu on the sun.  From the benchmarks,
I was expecting around at least a 3 times improvement in rendering speed.
We also passed our code through the KAP preprocessor on the DEC and it
didn't make much of an improvement on rendering times versus the non-
preprocessed.  

Just thought I would through in my two cents...


