In article <207v2k$8ce@news.acns.nwu.edu>, jweiss@casbah.acns.nwu.edu (Jerry Weiss) writes:
> We have a VS3100/30 that I was attempting to add some external
> SCSI stuff to, but the external connector has me confused.  We do
> not have any manuals for the thing.   Its a 68 pin mini-connector
> (w/terminator), and I'll guess that its a differential SCSI (II?)
> connector.  What cable (if any?) would I need to use this with a device
> using what I call a centronics type of connector.  Internally, there are
> two connectors on the scsi board.  One goes to the internal disk (on SCSI A).
> The other appears to be connected to the other SCSI chip (SCSI B?).
> Assuming that it is and that I use it, I'd further assume that I would
> need to terminate it after the last device.  

  It's weirder than that. It's not wide SCSI, it's not differential SCSI,
it's... ta-da! DEC SCSI!

  <Whimper>

  You need the BC56H-03 (3 feet) or -06 (6 feet) cable from DEC. This has
the weird connector on one end and a normal 50-pin "Centronics" style SCSI
connector on the other end.

  Assuming you have the SCSI/SCSI board (as opposed to SCSI/ST506), there
are 2 cable harnesses inside - a round one with 3 or 4 connectors on it,
which loops from the SCSI board around the "drive pan" and then back into
the same connector on the SCSI board, and a flat cable with 2 connectors
on it which also loops back to the same connector. The first (round) cable
is the SCSI A (internal) bus, and the second (flat) cable is the SCSI B
(external) bus. If the internal external cable (hey, this _is_ DEC 8-) is
missing, the external external bus won't work. You need a terminator on
the far end of the external external bus. If there are no devices, this is
provided by the 12-29635-01 terminator (which mates to the weird external
connector, but falls off if not held on by the 74-38189-01 cover).

  From your description, it sounds like you're missing the internal exter-
nal cable, which (if my IPB isn't lying to me) is part number 17-02212-01.
For reference, the round internal bus cable is 17-02231-01.

  All of the above-mentioned parts are available from DECdirect at 800-
DIGITAL, should you be so inclined...

  By the way, before you get all excited about adding your device, I'd make
sure it worked (especially if it's a tape) by sticking it on the internal
bus, before ordering all these parts.

