>'/media_format=compaction' implemented?  Should I use CRC?

You've asked religious questions -- if two people give you the same answer,
I'd be really surprised!

On my Exabyte 8500, I use /BLOCK=32256/CRC/GROUP=10.  I like the additional
insurance that /CRC gives me.  Yes, the tape does CRC checking, no, I've
never had it fail a CRC check, but for my site (a hospital) we need every
little bit of assurance that data being restored is the same as data that
was saved to tape.  If a backup begins to use up more than one tape, I
reduce the redundency groups until it begins to fit on one tape again.

The block size was chosen so the save-set can be copied to disk; 32256 is
the largest allowed record size on disk.

