Robert,

Digital does not discuss future product plans, except under terms of non-disclosure.  The design of the DEC 3000 Model 300 AXP family is based 
on CPU daughtercard technology, however it was primarily done to increase available board space in a minimum system footprint.

That said, there is no technical reason why different CPU/cache subsystems 
could not be implemented on these systems. In fact one of the differences between the Model 300L and the 300 is a different speed chip on the otherwise
identical CPU daughtercard.  Other differences exist on the mother board such 
as built-in video resolution and number of TURBOchannel slots.

