>that brings up another question:  i do have a modem connected to a
>DS200, but cannot get it to go faster than 9600 either.  i'd like to
>be able to set up the connection between the modem and the termserver
>at 19200, and allow the modem to negotiate.  i can't seem to get the
>termserver to lock in at 19200.  is this possible?

If you have any choice in the matter, lock the terminal server speed at
19200bps  (eg, disable autobaud).  That makes things much simpler.

This assumes that your modems can do asynchronous speed buffering.  If it can,
the terminal server certainly handles 19200 (that's what I'm using with several
Telebit modems).

