In article <C8H488.8ow@sdr.slb.com>, lovell@sdr.slb.com (John Lovell) writes:
>Hi. How does one terminate a Decwindow session!?? I am logging into a
>VAX from an SGI and running sys$system:decw$session with the DISPLAY
>[stuff deleted]
>
>My problem is TERMINATING the session. If I click "EndSession"
>then my whole terminal hangs. If I then log into the IRIS remotely from
>another machine and kill Xdm, then X restarts itself but now the words DIGITAL
>appear in big letters on my screen and I am invited to enter my password
>back on the VAX. The only thing that clears it is to reboot the IRIS.
>[stuff deleted]
>
As far as I know, firing off the Session Manager with the "End Session" means:
1.) send a "Reset" to the X-Server (which will do a "Kill all clients")
2.) start a Login Window (with the DIGITAL logo in the background).

My suggestion:
Customize your Session Manager "Session" menu to include a "Quit" like the
one in the File View "Control" menu.

Note that the "Quit" will then only stop the Session Manager and all of his
subprocesses, which are not necessarily all applications it started.

BTW The DEC session manager starts by default a window manager after login.
If you use the session manager on a remote X-server, it's better to disable
this feature and use a local window manager (here the SGI one) instead.
Your network will thank you.

-Peter
