I just posted version 1.1 of plan to alt.sources. Plan is a calendar
program with various appointment entry and alarm options. Since my first
posting four weeks ago, various features have been added, a few bugs have
been fixed, and it has been ported to more systems.

I also submitted the sources to the FU Berlin postmaster, who will make
them available for anonymous ftp on <fub@in-berlin.de>. I suggested to put
plan into ~ftp/unix/graphics; check out the INDEX.Z file (it was 70 KB
last time I looked). Give them a few days to install it. The plan sources
are some 430 KB uncompressed and 180 KB compressed.

The Subject in alt.sources is "X/Motif calendar/day planner/alarm clock
V1.1, part [0-7] of 7", msgid 1993Jun13.195929.23391@bitrot.in-berlin.de.


The updated sales blurb from the 1.0 posting:
---------------------------------------------

Plan is a schedule planner based on X/Motif. It displays a month calendar
similar to xcal, but every day box is large enough to show appointments
in small print. By pressing on a day box, the appointments for that day
can be listed and edited. Features include:

- the date, time, and length of the appointment
- an optional text message to be printed
- an optional script to be executed
- optional early-warn and late-warn triggers that precede the alarm time
- optional repetition information: weekdays, days-of-the-month, every n days
- optional fast command-line appointment entry
- a fancy holiday parser that can deal with moving holidays and vacations
- root access not required for installation

The action being taken when a warn or alarm time is reached is programmable;
by default a window pops up. In addition, a program can be executed, or mail
can be sent. Other methods of listing appointments (today, this week, next
week, or a keyword search for regular expressions) are also available. Plan
can be configured to display times in 12-hour or 24-hour formats, mmddyy and
ddmmyy date formats, and can show either Monday or Sunday in the leftmost
column.


The program now runs on the following systems:
----------------------------------------------

      SGI          All 4.x and 5.x SGI systems
      HP/UX 8.x    with X11R4 and Motif 1.1.5
      HP/UX 9.01   with X11R5 and Motif 1.2
                   (by Sylvain Picard <lmcsypi@LMC.ericsson.se>
                   and Lothar Paltins <lotharp@hpbidrd.bbn.hp.com>)
      OSF1/AXP     (by Dave Hill <ddhill@zk3.dec.com>)
      IBM/AIX      (by Johan Eksteen <johan@boer.ee.up.ac.za>
                   and Vance R. Bass <vrbass@vnet.IBM.COM>
                   and David W. Sanderson <dws@ssec.wisc.edu>)
      NCR          (by Keith Shafer <kshafer@cheers.sandiego.NCR.COM>)
      SUN          (by Dave Brennan <brennan@hal.com>
                   and Matthias Wilhelmi <wilhelmi@prosun.first.gmd.de>)
      ULTRIX 4.3   (by Jeroen C. Kessels <jeroenk@cnplss7.cnps.philips.nl>)

I merged all the patches I got for these new platforms as well as I could,
but some were mutually exclusive, and there seem to be many variations of
some systems, especially HPs and Suns. Complain to me if I made a mistake,
not to the people listed above who did the ports.

If you followup to this posting, please send me an email copy. Of all the
groups this posting is crossposted to, I only read comp.sys.sgi.apps; my
feed doesn't even include some of the other groups. Thanks!

Have fun,

Thomas
