We replaced a cluster of an 8700, two 8650s and two HSCs with a cluster 
containing a 4500 and two 4300s, and I would say that there is no 
problem as far as having enough I/O.  The cluster has three DSSIs (I think)
plus some more disks on a SCSI, and the I/O performance is significantly
much better than with the HSC cluster.  I suppose the improvement is due
to the RF's being much faster than the RA's (50-60 IOs/sec vs. 30 IOs/sec)
and to the fact that RF's, having autonomous controllers, scale better 
when multiple spindles on a single bus are active.

The 4500/4300/4300 cluster probably handles a load of 200-250 
concurrent users.  Whether a single 4400 could handle such a load is
somewhat doubtful to me ...

