Lines: 24

Error 72 means that there is something wrong with the controller.  I got
this information from the local Reno DEC service group.  The nice lady,
who I have known since we got our Vaxmates new, also told me that it
sometimes means that the cable connectors are loose.  This seemed like a
hot possibility to me, since I had fiddled with the slot assembly myself
in adding a modem.  I had also recently moved the Vaxmate from room to
room and could have jostled something loose.  I fixed the problem by
opening up the expansion box and pressing the connectors between the
controller card and the hard drive firmly together. 

There are a number of other error number messages that you can get by
booting up with an MS-DOS diskette and pressing <ctrl> and <alt> and
<home> at the same time. The home key in this case is the one that is <7>
on the num block.  Some of these are in the Vaxmate System Handbook that
came with the machines.  But, you still need the DEC technicians manual to
find out what they mean, or have a friend who owns that manual.  Another
valuable manual that used to be available to civilians is the Vaxmate
expansion box installation guide. 

Allen Gardner
University of Nevada, Reno





