===========================================================
I did this by having two copies of /etc/ttys; one called /etc/ttys.8 and
one called /etc/ttys.24, with the appropriate command to get the 8 bit
or 24 bit screen. Then I have two scripts which copy the desired ttys
file to /etc/ttys and executes /bin/kill -HUP 1:

#!/bin/sh
/bin/cp -f /etc/ttys.24 /etc/ttys
/bin/kill -HUP 1

The only problem with this is that the script has to be run as root,
which is a security hole, but it wouldn't be too hard to rewrite the
script as a C program that runs as root.

