In <36812@oasys.dt.navy.mil> timsmith@oasys.dt.navy.mil (Timothy Smith) writes:

>Hi.

>Our recently-moved MicroVAX II was, as far as I can figure, working
>fine yesterday afternoon.  This morning, it was powered up, but not
>responding to any terminals, including the console.

>When I reboot, the LED on the CPU's back panel counts down from 9 to
>2, and remains at 2.  No response to the console; no change when I've
>power cycled, switched console terminals, switched cables etc.  The
>power cycling did generate some backwards question marks on the console,
>but besides that, no response.

>Can anyone out there tell me what these numbers on the back panel display
>mean, or suggest anything to do besides call DEC field service?  Three
>shelves of blaze orange folders, and not one of them says a single useful
>thing....

	F	Electrical power up

	E	Wait for PWR ok

	D	Rom checksum ? & TOY RAM tests

	C	Init console prog memory

	B	Run IPCR tests

	A	Test & check for VCB01/2

	9	Console port & terminal ID

	8	console language ? enter console command mode

	7	Memory pattern tests

	6	Memory address tests

	5	I/O map tests

	4	CPU tests

	3	interrupt tests

	2	search for boot device

	1	Load bootstrap

	0	RUN

So your machine is looking for it's boot device.

By default this is "du0" (unless there is a TK50 loaded & online) so check
cables etc are in (especially relevant after a move ;-) and all the boards are
pushed in (& socketed chips if you are adventurous ;-)

Also it may be you type in another boot device ? this may mean your switches
at the rear have been changed, check them.

However you should see the "countdown" on the console also, if not it seems your
console is perhaps unplugged or sick (first check the console cable to the CPU
board in the back).

John

