In article <SINGHAL.93Jun2153622@twins.cs.utexas.edu>, singhal@twins.cs.utexas.edu (Vivek P. Singhal) writes:
|> [My apologies if this is a FAQ]
|> 
|> We have an assortment of DECstation 5000/{200,240,20}s running Ultrix
|> 4.2a.  We're considering upgrading to either Ultrix 4.3a or OSF/1.  I
|> am trying to determine the advantages / disadvantages of each option.
|> 
|> For us, one benefit of OSF/1 would be the ability to create
|> lightweight processes and exploit shared memory.  (Sanity check: does
|> OSF/1 indeed support these features?)
|> 

Yes, it does support these features.  I used OSF/1 on MIPS to build a threaded
version of Xlib.

|> I would like to find out what other peoples' experiences have been
|> with OSF/1 (especially those who have migrated from Ultrix):
|> 
|> 0) Is OSF/1 for the MIPS "officially" supported by DEC?  Will future
|>    versions of OSF/1 be supported for this architecture?
|> 

As far as anyone I've heard from goes, DEC has officailly "De-committed" to
OSF/1 on MIPS platforms.

|> 1) Can most freeware/shareware packages (GNU, X11, TeX) be compiled
|>    under OSF/1?  (Fortunately, we use almost no commercial software
|>    packages, so the availability of such programs for OSF/1 isn't
|>    really an issue).
|> 

I have been able to build many of the software packages available over the
net.  DEC is even distributing a "Freeware CD" for Alpha OSF/1.  OSF/1 has a
BSD compatibility switch for the compiler which allows most software configured
to compile on Ultrix to also compile on OSF/1.  Also, most programs compiled
for Ultrix will run on OSF/1.  Some network features don't work, but I haven't
really had any other problems.

|> 2) Is OSF/1 for the MIPS stable?  Is it still being distributed as a
|>    "developer's system", or it safe for daily use?
|> 

I have been using OSF/1 on MIPS for about 1.5 years now (pre-releases and the
1.0 release) and have found a few bugs in the include files and one or two
library routines.  I have not had any problems with the kernel itself but I am
not a really beating on it very hard (I write X/Motif programms for a living).

|> 3) Is OSF/1 significantly faster / slower than Ultrix?
|> 

OSF/1 is significantly slower than Ultrix.  Not sure why, but running a simple
csh loop showed OSF/1 to be much slower output (this is totally subjective, I
have never measured the difference).  The multi-threading libraries have also
demonstrated some performance problems.  I have not had the time to pinpoint the
problems but our tests of Xlib showed a significant (>2x) slow down when using
the threaded libc_r library.

|> 4) Is the administration of OSF/1 machines significantly different
|>    than administration of Ultrix machines?
|> 

System admin for OSF/1 systems looks much more like a hybrid SYS-V/BSD4.4 than Ultrix.  Lots of the sys admin files have moved and it uses run levels and an
inittab file instead of rc.local.

|> 5) Any other issues that should be considered when migrating to OSF/1?
|> 

DEC is now offering trade-ins on the MIPS boxes for Alpha systems.  No telling
how long these offers will be around.  If you have "lots" of systems and you
continue to be an active DEC customer, you might even be able to twist the
sales reps arm a little to get a better deal.  I would suggest threatening
legal action because you bought the systems after DEC promised that they would
support OSF/1 on MIPS ;-).

