I've been installing some of the available PD software for DEC Alpha
OSF/1 system, and I'd like to make a request of people who are porting
software to that platform:

  Please put your changes inside an #ifdef/#endif (or whatever the
  language the program is written in has that is similar).

The reason I ask this is that we support many architectures/platforms here,
and use a common source tree for programs that we install.  A fair amount
of the ported source code I have seen has just had the changes made to it
without surrounding #ifdef/#endif; that means I either have to remake the
changes to the copy of the sources that we have or keep two copies of the
sources around.  I am sure there are others in the same situation that we
are in, and they would appreciate it too.

In the programs I have had to tweak for the Alpha, I've used

  #ifdef __alpha

for 32/64 bit changes (usually int vs. long), and

  #ifdef __osf__

for OSF/1 specific changes.


