  Actually, it's filed in my filing cabinet under DLP-11 8-)

> The DLP-11 was a clone of DEC's LP11 Unibus line printer controller.
> I need documentation on the three blocks of DIP switches on this
> beast.  Can anybody help, please?  Don't ask ... :-( 

  Switch D4, positions 1 through 8 are address bits 12 through 5 (ON=0, OFF=1)

  Switch E4, positions 1 through 3 are address bits 4 through 2 (ON=0, OFF=1)
	     positions 4 through 8 are vector bits 7 through 3 (ON=0, OFF=1)

  Switch F3, position 1 is vector bit 2 (ON=0, OFF=1)
	     position 2 is long lines enable when ON (only if board has option)
	     position 3 must be OFF
	     position 4 selects centronics/dataproducts (OFF=Cen/LA180, ON=DP)
	     position 5 selects LA180 mode (ON=Cen/DP, OFF=LA180)
	     position 6 unused
	     position 7 Unix mode (ON=Unix, OFF=not Unix)
	     position 8 data bit 8 disable (ON=7 bits, OFF=8 bits)

  Note that this controller has some problems - if in Centronics mode, the
board won't respond to some OS's (like RSTS/E) sizing tests unless the prin-
ter is ready and on-line. Also, in Centronics mode you can't print binary
data (like PCL or similar) without a mod as the board wants to give you a
free <CR> before every <LF> or <FF>.

