I work in a heterogeneous, networked environment. I am looking for
a consistent way to determine, when connected to a machine other 
than the one I am in front of, which machine I came from. It
seems that every platform can retrive this information, but each
one does it differently.

In case I wasn't clear, if I'm sitting at machine A and rlogin into
machine B and then telnet into machine C, is there any way from machine
C to extract the fact that I connected from machine B? Similarly, from
B can I determine that I came from machine A?

There are various ways on different platforms such as the who command
on Sun and HP or the REMOTEHOST variable on IRIX. But where is this
generic information stored?

Thanks in advance for any responses. Please e-mail directly.

