X-Newsreader: TIN [version 1.1 PL9]

I have read in the DEC newsgroups that OSF/1 on MIPS will not me supported
by DEC... even after they told their customers that they would.  I am also
told... though less reliably... that there will be no new versions of Ultrix.
So, presumably, DEC is abandoning the MIPS based machines and, for RISC anyway,
going completely over to the Alpha systems with OSF/1 and OpenVMS.

It seems DEC has a very poor attitude toward their customers.  First they
promise to provide OSF/1 on the MIPS systems.  This promise must have
influenced customers decisions to purchase these machines.  Then, shortly
after announcing the release of the Alpha systems, they go back on that
promise.  Since some customers will have only recently purchased machines
and or software they will not be in a good position to upgrade to the new
systems.

It is my impression that what a number of customers will do is go to a
company that they believe will keeps it's word and provide them with support
for the machines they may have only recently purchased.  Support which they
must have expected at the time.  To me it looks as if DEC has shot itself
rather badly in the foot with this policy/attitude.  Can any company really
expect to behave in this way and survive??

Ian.


