              CUSTOMIZED MANAGEMENT FORUM PACKAGE FEATURED AT
                             DECUS '93/ATLANTA



SHREWSBURY, Mass., June 1, 1993 --  Information technology managers will be 
able to build a customized three-day management forum package at DECUS 
'93/Atlanta.  This is the first time the U.S. Chapter of The Digital 
Equipment Computer Users Society (DECUS) has offered a management-focused 
subset of the semi-annual national event.

From June 6-8, managers of information technology can participate in a 
management package that includes a one-day seminar, over 30 symposium 
sessions, the Digital Technology Center and trade show.

Participants can choose one of four day-long management seminars, which 
will be held on Sunday, June 6, at the Georgia World Congress Center in 
Atlanta, Ga.  Topics include:

* Advanced Disaster Recovery Contingency Planning:  Meeting Your Business 
  Needs 
* Effective Information System Design 
* Implementing Open Systems -- A Guide for Technical Managers 
* Software Metrics and Function Point Analysis

On Monday, June 7 and Tuesday, June 8, participants can attend Management 
Track symposium sessions.  These sessions feature over 30 
management-focused topics such as corporate downsizing, migration, asset 
management and disaster plan management.  

The management package includes admittance to the Digital Technology Center 
-- the largest integrated showing of Digital and Digital-related partners' 
products, services and technologies -- on June 7 and 8.  The Digital 
Technology Center gives attendees the opportunity to view and test products 
while meeting with developers, product managers and other experienced 
users.

Management package participants will also receive admission to the trade 
show on June 8.  This is the first time a trade show is being conducted at 
a DECUS national event.  Participants will be able to visit over 100 
independent vendor exhibits including Oracle Corporation, Ross Systems, 
SAS, SmartStar and WordPerfect.

Managers of information technology interested in participating in the 
Management Forum package can register on site at the Georgia World Congress 
Center for $450.

DECUS '93/Atlanta will feature a total of 100 full- and two-day seminars, 
and over 1,100 symposium sessions covering virtually every area of 
computing.

On-site registration will be conducted throughout the event week in Hall E 
of the Georgia World Congress Center.  For more information on DECUS 
'93/Atlanta call 1-800-DECUS55.

DECUS members solve their organizations' computing problems and stay 
informed abut industry issues and emerging technologies with the aid of the 
Chapter's semiannual national seminars, symposium and trade show event; 
regional conferences; local seminars program; Special Interest and Local 
Users Groups; electronic conferencing system; and public domain library.  

