      SIX DIGITAL EXECUTIVES TO PRESENT SESSIONS AT DECUS '93/ATLANTA 
         INCLUDING DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION PRESIDENT AND CEO 
                              ROBERT B. PALMER

           Charles Christ, Robert Jolls, Laurence Walker, William
           Demmer and Donald Harbert Additional Featured Speakers



SHREWSBURY, Mass., June 2, 1993 -- The U.S. Chapter of the Digital Equipment 
Computer Users Society (DECUS) today announced that six Digital Equipment 
Corporation executives, including Digital Equipment Corporation President 
and CEO, Robert B. Palmer, will present sessions at DECUS '93/Atlanta at the 
Georgia World Congress Center in Atlanta, Ga.  

In addition to Palmer, key executives speaking are:  Charles Christ, vice 
president, Storage Business Unit; Bob Jolls, vice president of Products and 
Services Marketing; Laurence Walker, vice president, Network Engineering 
Group; William Demmer, vice president, Computer Systems Group; and Donald 
Harbert, vice president, OpenVMS Engineering Group.

Palmer, who will deliver the keynote address, is expected to talk about the 
changes taking place at Digital and future directions the company is 
pursuing.  His address is scheduled for 8:00 a.m. on Tuesday, June 8 in the 
auditorium of the Georgia World Congress Center.  This is the first address 
made by Palmer to the U.S. Chapter of DECUS since becoming president in 
October, 1992.

The DECUS Networks Special Interest Group (SIG) will present a session given 
by Laurence Walker on Digital's network directions.  The address will begin 
at 10:00 a.m. on Monday in Ballroom 1.  

On Monday, June 7, the DECUS Business Practices SIG Support Group will 
present a session featuring Robert Jolls, at 11:00 a.m. in Room 167.  Jolls 
will discuss Digital's product transition program.

The DECUS Technology, Hardware and Engineering (T.H.E.) and VMS Systems SIGs 
will co-present "Storage Strategy Update," a special two-hour session 
featuring Charles Christ, also on Monday at 5:00 p.m. in the Georgia World 
Congress Center auditorium.  Christ will discuss how storage has changed 
dramatically over the past few years, where he believes storage is headed, 
and where Digital is headed in this ever-changing environment.  The session 
will include a question and answer period with Christ and a panel of 
Digital's storage engineers.

On Tuesday, June 8 at 9:00 a.m., the DECUS VMS Systems and Personal 
Computing SIGs will co-present "Digital's Operating Systems Strategy," 
featuring William Demmer.  This  session will provide attendees with 
strategic information on selecting an appropriate platform.  Also on 
Tuesday, at 10:00 a.m., Donald Harbert will discuss Digital's vision of 
OpenVMS features and functionality into the next century during a VMS 
Systems SIG-sponsored presentation. Both sessions will be held at the 
Georgia World Congress Center auditorium.

DECUS '93/Atlanta is a one-week event featuring a new multivendor trade 
show, 100 in-depth seminars and over 1,100 technical symposium sessions.  
The sessions and seminars run June 5-11 and the trade show runs June 8-10, 
all at the same location. 

On-site registration will be conducted throughout the event week in Hall E 
of the Georgia World Congress Center.  For more information on attending 
call 1-800-DECUS55.

DECUS members solve their organizations' computing problems and stay 
informed about industry issues and emerging technologies with the aid of the 
U.S. Chapter's semiannual national seminars, symposium and trade show event; 
regional conferences; local seminars program; Special Interest and Local 
Users Groups; electronic conferencing system; and public domain library. 

